P8-hardening-001 patch (outside the unit's write_scope; integrator applies). Rationale: the unit's gates need four
changes it may not commit. (1) subjects/egress-subject/Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock: the egress-tls-e2e gate builds
`-p egress-subject --features tls-client`, which needs a `tls-client` feature on the subject (monban-egress/tls-client,
optional monban-tls with tls-client, optional rustls for the CA store); off by default so ssrf-corpus and workspace
builds keep monban-egress without the rustls client; the lock gains only the two edges egress-subject -> monban-tls,
rustls (no new crate). The subject source using it is committed on the branch (src/ is in scope). (2)
subjects/state-subject/src/main.rs: the state-props retention case (IDEMP-R) needs `--idempotency-retention <s>`
(State::set_retention), `CLOCK <unix_s>` (State::set_clock), `PURGE` (State::purge_expired), `features=retention` on
READY and the advertised mutations retention-ignored / retention-early (monban-state hidden StateMutations) and
purge-noop. (3) gates/phase-8.toml egress-tls-e2e: `remote = "kamrui"` instead of the desktop: the upstream peer is
OpenSSL >= 3.5 (ML-KEM TLS groups); kamrui has 3.5.3, the desktop has 3.3.1 with no ML-KEM groups (probed
2026-11-06), so the gate cannot run there. No check is weakened by any hunk. Not included, for P8-bin-001 (single
writer of monban-bin): wherever monban-bin opens monban_state::State it must call
`state.set_retention(cfg.state().idempotency_retention_s)` and run `State::purge_expired()` periodically; until then
F8 state.idempotency_retention_s is parsed but not applied in the server (IDEMP-R holds trivially: never expire).
(4) crates/monban-config/tests/p8.rs (P8-spec-001): a blank doc line so clippy::doc_lazy_continuation (-D warnings) passes; workspace clippy with --all-targets fails on it at the branch base. Optional: fuzz/examples/seeds.rs has no pg_message seeds; the target's odd mode synthesizes framing, so it reaches
every message grammar from an empty corpus.
Verified on kamrui with this patch applied over the branch head (see the unit's final report).
Apply: git apply units/phase-8/patches/P8-hardening-001.patch

